es him as a Swiss journalist, consultant, artist and racing driver, born October 8, 1980. The Wikidata entry gives the same description and lists Zurich as his birthplace, with occupations including journalist, cabaret performer and comedian.\n\nHis motorsport record in the Wikipedia article is brief. It mentions a sixth-place finish at the 2000 Rwanda Mountain Rally in a Toyota, and his involvement with Team Porsche at the Eco Grand Prix and a 24-hour race at the Nürburgring in a Porsche Taycan.\n\nThe article's best-known item is a 2020 electric motorcycle record on a Harley-Davidson LiveWire, which covered 1,724 km in under 24 hours. Other coverage I found, including a German-language profile, gives the distance as 1,723 km, so the figures differ slightly by source."], "durationSeconds": 5.477877375, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01KR3K7G1KqQUxXBgTfpJVi1", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
